ng style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">TRANSFERS&nbsp;</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Airport Transfers using private AC vehicle</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tours &amp; Transfers using shared AC vehicle for the itinerary (not at disposal)</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">VISA&nbsp;</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">30-day single-entry tourist visa included</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">ATTRACTIONS &amp; TOURS</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dhow Cruise Creek with SIC Transfers</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Half Day Dubai City Tour with Burj Khalifa 124th Floor (Non-Prime Time tickets) with SIC Transfers</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Desert Safari with Dinner with SIC Transfers</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dubai Frame with SIC Transfers</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Museum of Future with PVT Transfers</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Yas Island 1 Day 2 Park Access- using Shuttle Service from </span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">City Seasons Towers Bur Dubai/Citymax Hotel Dubai/Howard Johnson by Wyndham Bur Dubai</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">EXCLUSIONS</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Airfare&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Option 1:(fare at the time of preparation of this quote is Rs 47,500 per person for AMD-DXB-AMD, however it will be booked on actual prevailing fare at the time of confirmation)&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXeh1GL4xLdW9lcMqRLy1SpEoBa4FGcrpCrut7sHwWvpJRP-Lm8EnI_5WieTwTFMVa1bvWEETV6WFtU3LW0A6vqKQcRYxH2uza2NvA7sTcRC1LGyaQ8uQsXfGP9il8fdJ5vBWhX__Ac3hgtDOQfAOPo?key=4sW0ziMIHk0_kvfRKc4Eyg\" height=\"82\" width=\"250\"></span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Option 2:(fare at the time of preparation of this quote is Rs 34,000 per person for BOM-DXB-BOM, however it will be booked on actual prevailing fare at the time of confirmation)&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfbNdam4WcVDoqkTxUQZ7ttjZ2fO_F40Iym9GqGFHqRIvWJIOQii2jfdZh0k_Je8HzvnfuZsfw5CwkaNnvCPX_pUEpcVDbrG4WEiPEUJ9skDptFcCR5X1_GsoUhKubquQ2kktgsl23xfHg8GvAXZKw?key=4sW0ziMIHk0_kvfRKc4Eyg\" height=\"76\" width=\"236\"></span></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tourism Dirham to be paid directly to hotel (AED 15-25 per day per room)</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">All kinds of personal expenses such as tips, laundry, telephone bills, beverages, etc</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Any parking &amp; toll charges for full day private vehicle at disposal</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Any meals &amp; beverages unless and otherwise specifically mentioned</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Additional sightseeing charges or extra usage of vehicle</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Any additional charges arising due to natural calamities, political disturbances, etc</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Anything else not specifically mentioned in the inclusions.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Mandatory TCS at 5% of Package Cost (as per RBI wef 1st&nbsp;Oct 2020, for all foreign remittances for travel outside India, a TCS of 5% is to be collected. A TCS Certificate against the same will be issued to traveler and the same can be claimed while filing ITR)</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">TOUR ITINERARY</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 1: ARRIVAL AT DUBAI, PICK UP TRANSFER, DHOW CRUISE</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Welcome to Dubai- The city of Gold!</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Upon arrival at Dubai, meet and greet at the airport and transfer to your hotel. Check In and some time to rest.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Later in the evening around 7PM, proceed for Dhow Cruise to experience something that is inexplicable and beyond your imagination with our 2-hour classy cruise. The Venetian styled canal will leave you and your loved ones impressed. This traditional dhow will offer you the best views of modern Dubai from the most unexpected angles. Witness the glorious architecture of Dubai that the world acknowledges while you feast on the international cuisines. An elegant and sophisticated setting will elevate your cruising experience and leave you with lovely memories to cherish for a lifetime. Entertainment will be arranged onboard, and you will be cruising while enjoying the savory dishes and drink. The stunning view, sumptuous meals and the live entertainment will give you a dazzling experience.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Return to hotel and overnight at hotel.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXe6mWotdrgv-RxVBa9bRDmPdA-35UxqZBHvbcoWIV1k8ETymRvkFUDD9c0L1oxnT_BBveum5aMVmyeR2x_7wcdseKLybvjvje7kSih7KChtaNpRkO_ortkjB08pq9gLqlDbZ7ZPEfQv9r1VvC-AJA?key=4sW0ziMIHk0_kvfRKc4Eyg\" height=\"369.5235455784199\" width=\"669\"></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 2: DUBAI CITY TOUR, DUBAI MALL, BURJ KHALIFA TOUR</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">In the morning after breakfast, proceed for a city tour of Dubai.</span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\"> </span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Our 4-hour Dubai city tour would take you to the most prominent places in Dubai. You also get to see two different sides of Dubai, the historical one and the modern one. Beginning with the Dubai Museum, located in the Al Fahidi Fort (built in the 18th century), you get to see Dubai before it discovered oil and became the power city it is today. This is followed by a drive along the Dubai Creek, which is a historical area and still holds remnants of the past. You get to enjoy Arabic architecture with a visit to Jumeirah Mosque, which is the only mosque in Dubai open to non-Muslims. So, make the most of it. While the historical part of the city is quite interesting, your Dubai city tour would not be complete if you do not see its modern side.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">The tour takes you Hotel Burj Al Arab (which is designed in the shape of a sail), the Palm Islands (largest artificial island in the world), Hotel Atlantis the Palm (the crowning glory of palm Jumeirah), Jumeirah Beach and Burj Khalifa (the tallest building in the world). The tour also includes a drive along the Shiekh Zayed Road so that you can take a look at the skyscrapers and magnificent buildings on both sides of the road.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Later at around 4PM proceed to enjoy the Dubai Mall.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">After this, make your way to the 124th floor of Dubai\'s Burj Khalifa, the tallest of all the buildings in the world, standing tall and proud amongst the other skyscrapers of the city. One of the major landmarks of the city, the interiors of the Burj is as majestic as the steely exterior. During the tour, you are shown a multimedia presentation about the history of Dubai as well as the story of the construction of the building. Once you have gathered information about this tall structure, you are taken to the 124th floor observation deck on the fastest elevator. Here you get a chance to have a 360-degree panoramic view of the entire city of Dubai.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXeeHEZqA4GsARIWySkRrJmIrSMmYeChh2W9u7XNatafJJJTJ43XbSxNz6FbIyNEaDtf0lKTWW8uulUgRhh-g2QeUADZzfSCcqeKfWvEExvOkNRgTkT8eF7wzwRaj4ayiNvdlZzm1mTL9pPYoofhyNM?key=4sW0ziMIHk0_kvfRKc4Eyg\" alt=\"A picture containing sky, outdoor, building, city\r\n\r\nDescription automatically generated\" height=\"447.48654752279253\" width=\"669\"></span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Later, at around 7PM, see the spectacular Fountain Show at the Lake beside Dubai Mall. This is an open to public show so just look for a comfortable spot at the edge of the lake and enjoy the mesmerizing musical extravaganza. After this you have time at leisure for dinner at Dubai Mall (at your own expense) and return to the hotel by 9PM.Overnight at the hotel.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 3: DUBAI DESERT SAFARI</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Later at around 2PM, proceed to enjoy Dubai Desert Safari. Our desert safari trip includes spending a few hours’ time in a Bedouin style tent, right in the middle of the desert. The tour begins with our vehicle picking you up from your hotel and driving you down to the outskirts of the desert. Once you arrive at the desert campsite, you can enjoy riding a camel, smoking a flavoured shisha, drinking the traditional Arabic coffee, enjoying the captivating belly dance and Tanura dance. Do not miss the chance to take some breath-taking pictures of the desert in your camera, especially during sunset. The colours of the setting sun on the sands would leave you mesmerized. Apart from this, you can try out the traditional costumes, get a henna tattoo and enjoy a delicious buffet dinner. After the dinner, you would be dropped back to your place of stay. Overnight at the hotel.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXf3QHNzoQYzBekvbrPGo4LLQkND1Te_UrCAk7CxPo-DmTIvNISKz4yBPo170ys2D7cbcDdqBOlq_Bm3VOlsX2A_WGmaoXfkuT6dDmGJGeLMidYc2c6NKcXJnuBa7YQWMowOpF0krcCgKH6epXMRPQQ?key=4sW0ziMIHk0_kvfRKc4Eyg\" alt=\"A picture containing dune\r\n\r\nDescription automatically generated\" height=\"351.22340862905406\" width=\"669\"></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 4:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DUBAI FRAME l MUSEUM OF FUTURE&nbsp;</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">After your breakfast, proceed to explore the Dubai frame: Standing tall at 150 m, Dubai Frame provides a bird’s eye view of the city\'s famous and spectacular skyline, you can experience the views of Old and New Dubai and see how the city has transformed to a one of a kind metropolitan.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXffg9TH2crgBbU2lNR43LLrQw8nwOICtmQguiDufCSFtorxLUIjY24a-6BHw7vpC1T1vjREfq1EOEoIHL2pWhaIdJbO_AvwKSr08PlfcSnoB63Vo7l1qSIADvSl9zqNLcquIWz8h82fLhFQcPuX8d4?key=4sW0ziMIHk0_kvfRKc4Eyg\" alt=\"A picture containing sky, outdoor, track, city\r\n\r\nDescription automatically generated\" height=\"418.9432157383002\" width=\"669.0000000000001\"></span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(40, 40, 40);\">Then proceed to the latest additions to the iconic architectural structures in Dubai- The Museum of Future. </span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">The Museum of the Future is an exhibition space for innovative and futuristic ideologies, services, and products. Located in the Financial District of Dubai, UAE, the Museum of the Future has three main elements: green hill, building, and void.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXduI3cPuUBiIliqe-RscCSMn_DO_rMCpeGCNhNhlNscfaAR_z0uVC_6mjQ3MEcPLD-lq46dJIfAYYmc7PNMbLdCukwDafFurEhKEgYzHMagTEYJMZ3FwZgl8LySXQmjaGG5IEgEpzHjx1QJRpoOTs4?key=4sW0ziMIHk0_kvfRKc4Eyg\" alt=\"A picture containing sky, grass, outdoor\r\n\r\nDescription automatically generated\" height=\"446.6286491415148\" width=\"669\"></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 5: YAS ISLAND </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">1 DAY 2 PARK ACCESS</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Today after an early breakfast, proceed to Yas Island, Abu Dhabi using free shuttle service from City Seasons Towers Bur Dubai/Citymax Hotel Dubai/Howard Johnson by Wyndham Bur Dubai </span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);\">(If you stay at any other hotel than this, you need to reach these hotels on your own to use the free Shuttle Service)</span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">. Visit any 2 Theme Parks from Ferrari World, Yas Waterworld Yas Island, Warner Bros. World Yas Island, SeaWorld Yas Island in a day and then return back to your hotel in Dubai using shuttle service.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcxgAT_biI_GT-n6JoMkoU7q1pzy-Mh9a7VNkyNIau7uWMiP24AZD5HLPsGdv8tNeUYsxp46NWmruM9mhasLtOTMl3-giFDc22G00g-QFSEAkwQk-FECxwiik5gnM6CcDLUxfX-EsnmGZ-toEdioVQ?key=4sW0ziMIHk0_kvfRKc4Eyg\" height=\"370.99539269259617\" width=\"705\"></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 6: DEPARTURE</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">After morning Breakfast time at leisure until checkout. After checkout proceed to the airport for your flight back home with happy memories.</span></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">VISA &amp; MANDATORY DOCUMENTS</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Visa is required for visiting Dubai. Documents needed for eVisa for Dubai</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">A passport valid for at least 6 months beyond the period of intended stay, containing at least 2 blank pages.</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Digital colour copy of your passport size photograph (43mm x 55mm) taken against a white background. Avoid blurred and unclear photos.</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">PAN Card</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Visa on arrival is available for Indian nationals with valid US, UK or Schengen Visa.</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">CANCELLATION POLICY</strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">FLIGHT (IF APPLICABLE):</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">As per airline policy and selected fare rules.</span></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">LAND PACKAGE:</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Visa Charges (Rs 7,500 per person): Non-refundable&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">25% Cancellation charges if cancelled anytime after confirmation but at least 30 days before travel date</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">50% Cancellation charges if cancelled within 30 days but before 15 days of travel date&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">100% Cancellation charges if cancelled on or within 15 days of travel date</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">PAYMENT POLICY</strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">FLIGHT (IF APPLICABLE):</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">100% Advance</span></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">LAND PACKAGE:</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">At the time of confirmation: 25% of package cost</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">On or before 30 days from date of travel: 25% of package cost</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">On or before 21 days from date of travel: Balance 50% of package cost + Applicable TCS&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">PAYMENT OPTIONS</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">1.&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Net Banking:</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Payments can be made via electronic transfer to account,</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp; &nbsp; Account Name: Funstay Services Pvt Ltd</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp; &nbsp; Account Number: 141705001550</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp; &nbsp; Bank Name: ICICI Bank</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp; &nbsp; IFSC Code: ICIC0001417</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp; &nbsp; Branch: Marathahalli, Bengaluru&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">2.&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Credit Card&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">(2.5 % additional gateway charges applicable. 3.5% for AMEX and International Cards)</span></p><p>3.&nbsp;<strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">EMI Option</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp;, please check with us if interested&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">4.&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">UPI Payment&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Scan QR Code below and pay using any UPI App&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp; &nbsp;<img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXezQlsA6jNjPqROtiMqV08sScskQo9qToTLX0tQEBcJMJczX3X3O1vhETuiEwzcz1atMICHzzbtixH0gDM54u26pyBb4gZCd7MMQmLPADJaFJwYiSIZGzeA2ksOhnOrJS0UIoijGvxlftuADHjX7A?key=4sW0ziMIHk0_kvfRKc4Eyg\" alt=\"Qr code\r\n\r\nDescription automatically generated\" height=\"94\" width=\"96\"></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">TERMS &amp; CONDITIONS</strong></p><ol><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">The shared quote is valid for next 48 Hrs.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">We are not holding any rooms and final availability will be as prevailing at the time of confirmation.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Standard Check in time at the hotel is 3PM and checkout time is 12PM. Early check in &amp; Late Check Out is subject to availability and at the sole discretion of the hotel.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">The itinerary is tentative, the days and timings may be changed depending upon availability.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">If any Vehicle is required apart from the mentioned itinerary, then extra charge will be applicable as per actual on the spot. Dinner or Shopping trips will be charged extra.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">In an unfortunate scenario of a guest turning COVID positive during the stay in Dubai, expenses related to quarantine and medical treatment, if any, will have to be borne by the guest. Funstay will not be responsible for facilitating the same and guests need to follow the advice in accordance with Dubai Govt guidelines.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Funstay is not responsible for any flight cancellation, rescheduling, delays etc.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Guests are required to check all details (Names, Dates, Resort &amp; Package Details) upon receipt of confirmed booking voucher and immediately highlight any errors in the same. While Funstay will try to accommodate any correction requests until the latest possible on best effort basis, we cannot guarantee the changes if the same is not brought to notice at the time of receipt of such vouchers.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">In case of cancellation due to Govt restrictions, rescheduling or refund will be processed as per resort/airline policy, service charges applicable.</span></li></ol><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\"><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span>Regards,</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Sweta Nanda</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Lead- Sales &amp; Operations</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Ph: +918296645830</span></p><p><br></p>',NULL,'2025-08-05 09:42:50','sent','<442f72a5-2b2e-e364-bc5e-945bfd3beb2a@funstay.in>','12402',1,'sweta.nanda@funstay.in','[\"booking@funstay.in\"]','[]'),(107,NULL,'ishant.agarwal@gmail.com','12409 l 6N7D Georgia l Ishant Agarwal l 2 Pax l 01st to 07th October 2025','<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Dear Ishant,</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">Greetings from Funstay.in and thank you for your interest in Funstay’s travel services.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Funstay Services Private Limited is an experiential travel service provider based out of Bengaluru, India. It also owns &amp; operates Funstay.in, the online booking platform for experiential travel services tailored around unique and niche stays. With over 2000 properties across 100+ locations across India, Funstay is one of the pioneers in this segment and is also amongst the fastest growing company in experiential travel segment in India. To understand more about Funstay, visit&nbsp;</span><a href=\"http://www.funstay.in/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(89, 143, 222);\">www.funstay.in</a><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;,&nbsp;y</span><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">ou can also go through our reviews at&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/pg/funstay.in/reviews/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 255);\">Facebook</a><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">&nbsp;or&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/place/Funstay+Services+Pvt+Ltd+-+Homestay+in+Coorg,+Ooty,+Ladakh,+Andaman+Tour+Packages/@12.9085926,77.649664,15z/data=!4m7!3m6!1s0x0:0xf78d7e9aae2673f5!8m2!3d12.9085922!4d77.6496725!9m1!1b1\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 255);\">Google</a><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(17, 17, 17);\">.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">We are pleased to share below offers for your planned holiday in Georgia as below,</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">TRAVEL DETAILS</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Arrival Date: 01st Oct 2025</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">End Date: 07th Oct 2025</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">No of Nights: 6N7D</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">No of Guest: 2 Adults&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">No of Rooms: 1 Room&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Meal Plan: Breakfast</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0); color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">LAND PACKAGE COST(ALL TRAVELLERS): INR 1,30,000/- + 5% TCS + 5% GST</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">INCLUSIONS</strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">HOTELS, ROOM &amp; MEAL PLAN</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">In Tbilisi: </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">City Avenue Hotel</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(4 Star)</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">In Batumi:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> Courtyard by Marriott Batumi (5 Star)&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">E-VISA</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">TRANSFERS:</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Return Airport Transfers</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tours and transfers on Private basis by Giorgi | Toyota Camry | Sedan | 2010&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">A 4x4 car from Stepantsminda to Gergeti Trinity Church and back.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Entry fees according to the itinerary</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">TOURS:</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Full Day Tbilisi City Tour</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ananuri, Gudauri, Kazbegi Tour</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Prometheus Cave &amp; Martvili Canyon Day Tour</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Batumi city tour + Botanical Garden Tour</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Batumi- Makhuntseti Waterfall</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">ENTRANCE FEES</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tbilisi Cable Car+ Tram Ride, Prometheus cave &amp; Martvili Canyon Entry tickets + Boat tour in Martvili, Batumi Botanical Garden entry ticket&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">EXCLUSIONS&nbsp;</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Flights</span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\"> (fare at the time of preparation of this quote is Rs 60,000 per person, however it will be booked on actual prevailing fare at the time of confirmation)</em></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdo-zIgW1qhEGUTPHb-il3vj8oGjYLQ8OuP1tRg-oDAUJ4Dri-1_ENboBUvbM-Az4m9OEdF_zVwGWA9sznLPFIyUyGxRsiKQS33425qg5L-Z9j1T-QhcWJM8qb6_mQXGB1o21113C0xMnRTv2EID9I?key=QXDfUwx6kv0eyfz4KkE67Q\" height=\"89\" width=\"234\"></span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Any expenses of personal nature</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Early check in and Late check out</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Any meals &amp; beverages outside stated meal plan</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Anything else not specifically mentioned in the inclusion.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Applicable 5% GST</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Mandatory TCS at 5% of Package Cost (as per RBI wef 1st&nbsp;Oct 2020, for all foreign remittances for travel outside India, a TCS of 5% is to be collected. A challan against the same will be issued to a traveler and the same can be adjusted while filing ITR)</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">TOUR ITINERARY</strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 01: ARRIVAL IN TBILISI&nbsp;</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Arrival at the airport. After completion of all the immigration formalities transfer to the hotel. Check in and relax. Overnight stay in the hotel.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXedLT5disBVVuKX3FSnHGs5NRTd6KgAt2u8LeaXM_5mrq16KT-QHJeKjWK0VQ_-TXoKrmbaT87WOOh_lWggmqE02MP6hJD-ZNSQmhPuinL9jbF1ZB0VebTJMeNBzgsYn2yhBfdRPl2gxE_Jfajv7uE?key=QXDfUwx6kv0eyfz4KkE67Q\" height=\"466.537073035268\" width=\"699\"></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 02: FULL DAY TBILISI CITY TOUR (45KM, 8HRS)</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">10:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - You will meet the Driver and Guide in your hotel lobby and tour will start</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">10:20</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - you will reach Tbilisi and have a local tour. You will explore </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Metekhi church</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> and the monument to King Vakhtang Gorgasali, the legendary founder of Tbilisi. Walk down to the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Rike Park</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> and Cross the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Peace Bridge</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">. Take a cable</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> car </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">from Rike Park to </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Narikala Fortress</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> to enjoy a breathtaking panoramic view of the city and statue of </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Mother Georgia</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> standing above the old Tbilisi.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Walk down to the district of </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Sulphur baths</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> passing by the only </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">mosque</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> in Tbilisi. Stroll through the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Meidan Square</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> area full of narrow streets with cozy cafés, wine tasting bars, souvenir shops, and breathe in the living past.&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">13:00 </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">- Lunch Break&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">14:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - Mtatsminda Park- famous amusement park that overlooks the city Tbilisi- Breath taking views to city centre.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">17:00 Pm </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">&nbsp;– </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Chronicles of Georgia </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">- Famous sculpture in suburban area of Tbilisi&nbsp; - overlooking a Tbilisi water reservoir (known as Tbilisi sea)&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">18:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> -Transfer to hotel</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tour Attractions:</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Trinity church //Bridge of peace// Metkehi Church// Narikala fortress (by Cable Car)// Statue of Mother Georgia// Abanotubani (Sulphur Bath District)// Leghvtakhevi Waterfall // Mtatsminda park&nbsp; // Tbilisi Water reservoir//Chronicles of Georgia&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfRCdBu_GDxFiDz92AbITrKzg1ygGkW4_Hpbptm6h5Khimg2-fIldRXkIoPYa42XgRiawrizosURsB9vWdaYPmaMIfqLZafznlT7lbTo07vSU56TJZuJwMCXuXNKkx-A7n0qAIaHQNslKDMNmV9Ew?key=QXDfUwx6kv0eyfz4KkE67Q\" height=\"467.0561181494865\" width=\"699\"></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 03: ANANURI | GUDAURI | KAZBEGI (328 KM, 9HRS)</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">09:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - Checkout and meet the Driver and Guide in your hotel lobby, the route will take over the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Georgian Military Highway up North</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">, towards the border with Russia.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">10:30</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - You will reach </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Jhinvali Water reservoir</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> created during the soviet era. You will spend 20 minutes there and promptly continuing your way to </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Ananuri complex,</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> a former residence of Argveti Dukes.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">11:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - You will reach Ananuri complex. The complex features churches and towers dating back to the 16-17th centuries, beautifully overlooking the Jhinvali reservoir. Because of local uprising and clashes Ananuri was controlled by different Dukes. In the complex you will see two churches from 17th century. The older one was built in 1689 and has sophisticated ornaments of grapes and crosses symbolizing soul of Georgian culture.&nbsp; You will spend about 40 minutes there.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">11:30</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - Continue your drive to see the conjunction of two </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">small mountain rivers</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> famous for the fact that being different in color they still keep their own colors even after merge. Continuing on the way you will have a chance to taste the mineral mountain springs in Mleta.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">13:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">&nbsp; - You will reach </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Gudauri</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> and spend about 2-3 hours there. We will&nbsp; drive over the Cross Pass and make a short stop at the Soviet-era </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">“People’s Friendship” </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">mountain view point overlooking a deep gorge of Caucasus mountain range.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">14:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - After arriving to </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Kazbegi(Stepantsminda)</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> we will change our vehicle to a four-wheel drive car to reach </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Gergeti Holy Trinity Church l</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">ocated on altitude of 2170 meters, and enjoy breathtaking views of Mt Kazbegi</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">16:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - Transfer to </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Tbilisi</strong></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">18:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">&nbsp; - End of the tour&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tour Attractions:</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ananuri Fortress// Jhinvali Water reservoir// Georgian Military Road// Soviet-Georgian Friendship Monument// Town of Stepantsminda// Gergeti Monastery</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXd9AzdqIynnSF1S7iWmqKO33lX4M-5q30pOEfDSpeixe4eitLdmkvLkJHrwd7bgG-KIvbsPKKNOIPraGf_sYCdS1ZgfdNAhXCRMnOoYXSJXW2VH_gro5KnZDYWx72vdGV17Z0saOqIZAfHqkRv8Hgc?key=QXDfUwx6kv0eyfz4KkE67Q\" height=\"467.0568299941618\" width=\"699\"></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 04: TBILISI- PROMETHEUS CAVE &amp; MARTVILI CANYON- BATUMI (425KM, 10HRS)</strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;09:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> - You will meet the Driver and Guide in your hotel lobby and tour will start</span></p><ul><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">13:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - The tour starts with </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Prometheus cave</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">. There are 22 halls found, where just 6 halls are open for tourists. It is possible to walk through the length of 1420 meters in the cave\'s territory, visit the halls and enjoy time there.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Discover real masterpieces of nature - stalactites and stalagmites at Prometheus Cave, which are the most beautiful forms created by nature. While visiting the cave, hanging waterfalls are waiting for you</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">15:00 PM </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">&nbsp;You will reach </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Martvili </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">and explore </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Martvili Canyon </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">which offers a splendid and unique environment. It is 2400 m in length and 20-40 m in depth with a 12 meter high waterfall in the middle of the canyon.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Here you will encounter fossilized bones of animals inhabiting the land in pre-historic era. Additionally, there are traces of primary human in several grotto of canyon. Once, serving as a bath place for royal Dadiani family, today Martvili Canyon attracts people by its spectacular view, sparkling waterfalls and vibrant green subtropical nature.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">17:00 PM</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> Lunch break&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">20:00 PM </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Overnight in Batumi</span></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tour Attractions:</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Prometheus cave, Martvili canyon</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfQdzcqXuKE_ecbsJ1WriGWjBjjoCt744c4_7nYNU5T4XEkG0e_nSQXP4hJ4L_RCe6gj2ZyCGjJg7Ot3Zv_F5Q3Y4_z1n1bqUi09JfAzLE7s0Vo9Ty9bRNokJDX14Bn4tDXXsFay0RLH2aJ8J40GbA?key=QXDfUwx6kv0eyfz4KkE67Q\" height=\"446.2748629393225\" width=\"669\"></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 05: BATUMI CITY TOUR + BOTANICAL GARDEN (70KM, 7HRS)</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">10:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - You will meet the Driver and Guide in your hotel lobby and start the tour.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">10:40</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> – You will reach </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Batumi Botanical Garden.</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">&nbsp; Boasting one of the widest varieties of flora in the world, Batumi Botanical Garden was established in 1912 by the prominent botanist and geographer Andrey Krasnov. The garden is 111 hectares and contains flora from nine phyto-geographic areas. You will spend there about 1 hour</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">12:20</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> – You will reach Batumi city and have local tour. Batumi is the largest city of region. An outstanding architecture of Batumi, its statues, palm trees, nature resorts, amusement parks, unique and stylish cafes, pubs, bars and night clubs create an amazing atmosphere in the whole City.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">The places you will visit includes </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Europe Square</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">, where decorative, historical and modern buildings come together as one;&nbsp; Alphabetic Tower, which is a 130 meters high, modern steel sculpture shaped as DNA molecule and depicting unique </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Georgian alphabet</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">; the sculpture of </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Ali and Nino</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">,</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">portraying the love story of young people from different cultural and religious backgrounds; </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Batumi Ferris Wheel</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">, offering the panoramic view of the whole city, decorated with numerous light patterns which are illuminated at night; </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Piazza</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">, located in historical district of the city where the narrow streets are covered in the cobble stones all around, along with local cafes, pubs and bars.&nbsp; You will spend there about 4 hours(including lunch time)</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">17:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> – End of the tour</span></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tour Attractions:</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Botanical Garden // Europe Square // Alphabetic Tower // Statue of Medea // Statue of Ali and Nino // Batumi Ferris Wheel // Piazza Batumi</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdqWwS4OF_L9uEgF64EetI2xzuEjrVBZRBab5zhHHX3rNW3dH1_W9VU-TE2xHfXTwbV9fTrs283x4toqYPK4AsmO6A1yClHy6y5fdUhdpT9Ic4f9JE84XfFArX5t0RHzPP_KeFH2q5y7fCR_9E9f7A?key=QXDfUwx6kv0eyfz4KkE67Q\" height=\"292\" width=\"699\"></span></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 06: BATUMI- MAKHUNTSETI WATERFALL- TBILISI (430 KM, 9HRS)</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">11:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - You will reach Makhuntseti waterfall. It is one of the most popular waterfalls in Georgia. It is located in Adjara, in the Makhuntseti village. You can visit the Makhuntseti waterfall at any period of the year. Here you can also buy the locals’ natural products: honey, Churchkhela and so on… on the way there is also fast food.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">13:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - Departure to Tbilisi</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">20:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - End of the tour</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tour Attractions:</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Makhuntseti&nbsp; Waterfall // Makhuntseti village</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcTzAf7KNYxOkbGGL-1PjSUt5ntl5s65_8oBusIopsGVtPbuJLkJ6y5XyiKeT4mQGIlWNZOI7gXi0anEUgL26s7xMbmg4N6kSVnfM5CsQ_NVgJuKmtkWKr_xP_H10G6NxuE6psX4jKJ49gT7e1nl0k?key=QXDfUwx6kv0eyfz4KkE67Q\" height=\"466.920321758659\" width=\"699\"></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 7: DEPARTURE</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Breakfast at the hotel. Time at leisure to explore on your own. Transfer to the airport for the flight back home with sweet memories of your holiday.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">CANCELLATION POLICY</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Flight: As per the Airline Policy</span></p><p><span style=\"b