e=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">A 4x4 car from Stepantsminda to Gergeti Trinity Church and back.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">TOURS:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Full Day Tbilisi City Tour</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Bodbe, Sighnaghi Tour</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ananuri, Gudauri, Kazbegi Tour</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Gudauri Local Tour</span></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">ENTRANCE FEES</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tbilisi Cable Car&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">EXCLUSIONS&nbsp;</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Flights </span><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">(fare at the time of preparation of this quote is Rs 53,700/- per person, however it will be booked on actual prevailing fare at the time of confirmation)</em></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfp0cowFsZWlDUyF4o8Phq1B-eo1eF5C3krBTf5b0JbeCXKFNxh0ncqDMcP7JjU9mJaWN9VThd3g9YubgsKRF_v7RzuGRQIrvBSM3FlptWEO9E_mkhjTzNDRg4pk75kaEfTgEYwtOr2tYn1ri2udw?key=54dUERAILZfi56DXBhEWXA\" height=\"83\" width=\"250\"></span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Any expenses of personal nature</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Early check in and Late check out</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Any meals &amp; beverages outside stated meal plan</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Anything else not specifically mentioned in the inclusion.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Applicable 5% GST</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Mandatory TCS at 5% of Package Cost (as per RBI wef 1st&nbsp;Oct 2020, for all foreign remittances for travel outside India, a TCS of 5% is to be collected. A challan against the same will be issued to a traveler and the same can be adjusted while filing ITR)</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">TOUR ITINERARY</strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 01: ARRIVAL IN TBILISI | DAY AT LEISURE&nbsp;</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Arrival at the airport. After completion of all the immigration formalities transfer to the hotel. Check in and relax. Overnight stay in the hotel.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXc5psU0WVvgWqvGip0YrF_hZTnYF6GpqyPRz0-CP0P5vc7hkjmjD5mNiGPFz2PQ8RIOh0dYy45r4mRVXeUsevPkq8kfyvleAYtTet5xiiur7xHcIzzJ0KLfQ9QZfdbounaM66lG6PvPW6BqU01WBJg?key=54dUERAILZfi56DXBhEWXA\" height=\"466.3876577147005\" width=\"699\"></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 02: FULL DAY TBILISI CITY TOUR (60KM, 4HRS)</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">09:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - You will meet the Driver and Guide in your hotel lobby and the tour will start. You will explore </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Metekhi church</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> and the monument to King Vakhtang Gorgasali, the legendary founder of Tbilisi. Walk down to the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Rike Park</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> and Cross the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Peace Bridge</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">. Take a cable</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> car </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">from Rike Park to </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Narikala Fortress</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> to enjoy a breathtaking panoramic view of the city and statue of </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Mother Georgia</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> standing above the old Tbilisi.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Have lunch.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Walk down to the district of </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Sulphur baths</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> passing by the only </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">mosque</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> in Tbilisi.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Visit </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Leghvtakhevi Waterfall</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> behind the bath district.&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Sioni Cathedral</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> -officially the Cathedral of the Dormition of the Virgin Mary, is a historic Georgian Orthodox church originally built in the 6th7th centuries, extensively rebuilt in the 13th century, and served as the main cathedral and seat of the Catholicos-Patriarch of Georgia until 2004, now housing the sacred Cross of St. Nino among its relics.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">See the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">whimsical Gabriadze Puppet Theater</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> and</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> Clock Tower.</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Short walk or drive along </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Rustaveli Avenue</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">, home to theaters, museums, galleries, and the Parliament building.&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Anchiskhati Basilica</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> -Anchiskhati Basilica, built in the 6th century, is the oldest surviving church in Tbilisi and a remarkable example of early Georgian Christian architecture.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Transfer to hotel</span></li></ul><p><em style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Optional: Boat ride on the Mtkvari River at additional cost (if weather and time allow).</em></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tour Attractions:</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Metekhi church // King Vakhtang Gorgasali Monument // Rike Park // Tbilisi Mosque // Meidan Square // Shardeni Street// Gabriadze Puppet Theater &amp; Clock Tower // Sioni Church // Anchiskhati Basilica //</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXczTC-vLmZjaGQ1K7AwCAOBLcbEmnNppSt7r8sRG0DE4jvl0o4wYbQGCLU40wAc4ccQEdDTvlhmuruNkw5TKeft_dQbAfxqCQ4rjlSvy3XbwYkl0-dzqBBNXpDSyTdf0sG4qnum5XYkPij9zCKOTDU?key=54dUERAILZfi56DXBhEWXA\" height=\"467.0561181494865\" width=\"699\"></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 03: TBILISI- BODBE/SIGHNAGHI-TBILISI (235KM, 6HRS)</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">09:00 AM-</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> You will meet the Driver and Guide in your hotel lobby and start the tour.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">10:00 AM-</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> You will visit a Georgian style winery in Paterdzeuli.&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">12:30 PM-</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> Your first stop will be in Bodbe monastery complex functioning as a nunnery since 1889, which according to the legend is a burial place of St. Nino, who converted Georgia to Christianity in the 4th century (you will spend about 40 minutes there)&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">13:20 PM-</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> You will reach Sighnaghi, the city of love and the Royal Town, one of the crossroads of the Great Silk Road surrounded by defensive walls with 23 towers. You will spend about 2 hour there (including lunch break) and continue your tour.&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">16:00 PM-</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> Transfer to Tbilisi&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">18:00 PM-</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> End of the tour.&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Note: You can have a stop in the village of Badiauri, where you can buy famous Georgian breasts and take part in the bread making activity. This is on request and you can ask the driver in advance.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tour Attractions:</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Trip through Wine Region// Kakheti/Bodbe Monastery //City tour of Sighnaghi</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcaJaKEo_GyMyYl3Ti6jyA1902HQD3gjo-5OfFwJoI0MIX6n7XB_ouOE8BJFXdOpwN4s3wdZeYSZkMbr2XWEYSuIVGvk2f3WMu97atRKC6BmxJ96PtpW2Uo9V4uzvBC59mAPsVx1c4DvrRCtiZEic0?key=54dUERAILZfi56DXBhEWXA\" height=\"343\" width=\"699\"></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 04: DAY AT LEISURE</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 05: ANANURI | GUDAURI | KAZBEGI (250 KM, 7HRS)</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">09:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - Checkout and meet the Driver and Guide in your hotel lobby, the route will take over the </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Georgian Military Highway up North</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">, towards the border with Russia.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">10:30</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - You will reach </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Jhinvali Water reservoir</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> created during the soviet era. You will spend 20 minutes there and promptly continuing your way to </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Ananuri complex,</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> a former residence of Argveti Dukes.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">11:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - You will reach Ananuri complex. The complex features churches and towers dating back to the 16-17th centuries, beautifully overlooking the Jhinvali reservoir. Because of local uprising and clashes Ananuri was controlled by different Dukes. In the complex you will see two churches from 17th century. The older one was built in 1689 and has sophisticated ornaments of grapes and crosses symbolizing soul of Georgian culture.&nbsp; You will spend about 40 minutes there.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">11:30</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - Continue your drive to see the conjunction of two </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">small mountain rivers</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> famous for the fact that being different in color they still keep their own colors even after merge. Continuing on the way you will have a chance to taste the mineral mountain springs in Mleta.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">13:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">&nbsp; - You will reach </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Gudauri</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> and spend about 2-3 hours there. We will&nbsp; drive over the Cross Pass and make a short stop at the Soviet-era </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">“People’s Friendship” </strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">mountain view point overlooking a deep gorge of Caucasus mountain range.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Have lunch.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">14:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - After arriving to </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Kazbegi(Stepantsminda)</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> we will change our vehicle to a four-wheel drive car to reach </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Gergeti Holy Trinity Church l</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">ocated on altitude of 2170 meters, and enjoy breathtaking views of Mt Kazbegi</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">16:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> - Transfer to </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Gadauri</strong></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">17:00</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">&nbsp; - End of the tour&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Have Dinner and Transfer to hotel</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Note: 4x4 vehicles for the Kazbegi (Gergeti) must be selected separately under extra services. One of the main attractions of this tour is Gergeti Trinity Church, which can only be visited by taking a 4x4 vehicle from Stepantsminda to Gergeti.</span></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tour Attractions:</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">*Ananuri Fortress&nbsp; *Jhinvali Water reservoir&nbsp; *Georgian Military Road&nbsp; *Soviet-Georgian Friendship Monument &nbsp; *Town of Stepantsminda&nbsp; *Gergeti Monastery</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXeE4bBMZ8DDm1wYMIxubG3t5mK_PLWFQoEtQxgSMafMT9crX8GavK-z8slhR1qG1l2J6JBtDhPyLqBUCP8Beyy5-Q_oL-dBSx2H6wF8slzALcwgAETbc3EdQGB5wlpbSWrQP32TfYY52N5iYSJ-HWw?key=54dUERAILZfi56DXBhEWXA\" height=\"467.0568299941618\" width=\"699\"></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 06: GADAURI LOCAL TOUR (5 KM, 6HRS)</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">11:00 AM-</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> Tour will start at 11AM. Driver and guide will take you to Gudauri Friendship Monument. We will drive over the Cross Pass and make a short stop at the Soviet-era \"People\'s Friendship\" mountain view point overlooking a deep gorge of Caucasus mountain range.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">The guide will help you to explore Gudauri. In case of good weather guide will take you to paragliding spots, in case of snowy season guide will lead you to places where you can have skiing and snow mobile experience&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">There are a lot of activity options in Gudauri that can diversify your trip, starting from horse riding, quadrosicles to paragliding, snowmobile, snowboarding and lot more.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Local tour can last till 5-6 Pm, defending on activities you want to do during this day.</span></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tour Attractions:</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;Gudauri resort// Paragliding spots //Skiing spots // Friendship Monument&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXe9G_RNgpYdHYV2E1zoAl5pBuqKVKjilfYLZ7myleaerzhABo_SCnvjRyGgkikPcyvXW2oju12bJKlp2CHY8HxKWNkKmF9R8A-hIoHjHZLg_C3B4m2ic-BMROi3wYVoiYfQjny7kyP_W0gJhegpquw?key=54dUERAILZfi56DXBhEWXA\" height=\"467.1410919702051\" width=\"699\"></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DAY 7: DEPARTURE</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Breakfast at the hotel. Time at leisure to explore on your own. Have lunch and ransfer to the airport for the flight back home with sweet memories of your holiday.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">CANCELLATION POLICY</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: r