wo Toyota Crysta (with bucket seat)\n>\n>\n>\n> Kindly confirm.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Thanks and regards,\n>\n> Aria\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Ohri,Aria\n> *Sent:* Monday, September 1, 2025 12:44 PM\n> *To:* booking@funstay.in; nitin@funstay.in\n> *Subject:* Car Bookings for MicroPort Shanghai Team (7th & 8th Sep)\n>\n>\n>\n> Hi Nitin,\n>\n>\n>\n> This is with regards to our discussion regarding making the car booking\n> arrangements for our team.\n>\n>\n>\n> The itinerary is as follows:\n>\n> *7th Sep -* Pick me up from my home at 2pm (Rich Bouquet Building, 19\n> Hutchins Rd, 2nd Cross, Cooke Town) and then we will goto Pickup the\n> guests from T2 airport (6 bags 28inch Standard size)\n>\n> Take them to hotel for checkin to the hotel Lemon Tree Ulsoor\n>\n> Then some sightseeing in Bengaluru followed by dinner\n>\n>\n>\n> *8th Sep -* Pickup me from my home at 9am and then pickup guests with\n> bags from hotel Lemon Tree Ulsoor (there will be 6 bags 28inch Standard\n> size)\n>\n> Goto Bommasundra Industrial Area (Address: Innvolution Healthcare, Plot\n> No. 143A, Bommasandra Industrial Area, Bengaluru)\n>\n> Leave for T2 airport by 3pm.\n>\n>\n>\n> Based on our discussion, we can book the following:\n>\n>    1. 7th Sep – One Sedan and One Toyota Crysta (without bucket seat)\n>    2. 8th Sep – Need to book 9 seater Toyota Commuter – Please note we\n>    will have around 6 standard size 28inch bags. So trust that it will all fit\n>    in this Toyota Commuter. Please confirm.\n>\n>\n>\n> Please let me know the final charges and you can go ahead with the booking.\n>\n>\n>\n> Thanks and regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> *Rtn. Aria Ohri*\n>\n> *Regional Business Director (South Asia & Southeast Asia)*\n>\n> *MicroPort NeuroScientific Corporation*\n>\n> 1661 Zhangdong Road, Zhangjiang High-tech Park, Pudong New District,\n> Shanghai, PRC\n>\n> Mobile: +91 9833097171\n>\n> Email: Aria.Ohri@microport.com\n>\n> Website: https://microportneuro.com/\n>\n>\n>',NULL,'2025-09-01 10:16:52','received','<CA+w5kXjgoMKKiAmDnM4A7CyJkT0QdCcd5L2vQ5KOpv0idrBkgA@mail.gmail.com>','11576',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(137,NULL,'puspak.das@funstay.in','Parking Problem during Office Hours','Hi Sir,\n\nAs conveyed earlier, I\'m writing this mail to communicate officially to bring to your notice that we\'re facing a problem to park our bikes in front of our office.\n\nRK Tent House person keeps their van parallelly to their shop extending to Riddhi-Siddhi shop. If we sometime ask them to give us some space, they don\'t even bother to speak politely. The guy who smokes beedi downstairs is the rudest one. Then, we end up parking our vehicles somewhere else where we don\'t know if someone comes and scratches our vehicles.\n\nI request you to find a solution to this matter on priority as we can\'t continue to park our vehicles at other places.\n\nThank You!\n\n\nRegards,\n\nPuspak Das\n\nSenior Associate - Sales & Operations\n\nPh: 8296494654\n\nDISCLAIMER: This communication is confidential and may be legally privileged. If you are not the intended recipient; (i) please do not read or disclose to others, (ii) please notify the sender by reply mail, and (iii) please delete this communication from your system.\n\nFunstay Services Private Limited\n\n1192/1, 22nd Cross, 24th Main, HSR Layout Sector 2, Bengaluru - 560102\n\nPhone:   +918287039039, E-Mail: booking@funstay.in\n\nwww.funstay.in<http://www.funstay.in/>',NULL,'2025-09-12 05:43:30','received','<SEZPR06MB6958CB659ADBF863251B2745FA08A@SEZPR06MB6958.apcprd06.prod.outlook.com>','11777',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(138,NULL,'allysachin@gmail.com','we need tour package with flight and visa for vietnam and singapore','we need tour package with flight and visa for vietnam and singapore\n\n4A, 2 Kids (10 year, 3 yrs)\n\n### *Day 1 – 2 Nov (Delhi → Hanoi)*\n\n* Morning: Arrival & check-in at Old Quarter.\n* Afternoon (doable in half-day):\n\n  * *Ho Chi Minh Complex* (house-on-stilts, museum, One-Pillar Pagoda)\n  * *Temple of Literature* (Vietnam’s first university)\n* Evening:\n\n  * *Hoan Kiem Lake + Ngoc Son Temple + Huc Bridge*\n  * Skip Quan Thanh Temple (too much in half day, far from others).\n  * *Water Puppet Show* (book in advance).\n\n---------\n\n### *Day 2 – 3 Nov (Halong Bay Day Trip)*\n\n* Early morning: Drive Hanoi → Halong (\\~2.5–3 hrs).\n* Cruise from *Tuan Chau Harbor*:\n\n  * *Sung Sot Cave (Surprise Cave)*\n  * *Bo Hon Island*\n  * *Kayaking or Bamboo Boat*\n  * *Ti Top Island (panoramic view & beach swim)*\n* Evening: Return to Hanoi.\n\n---------\n\n### *Day 3 – 4 Nov (Hanoi → Da Nang → Hoi An)*\n\n* Early morning: Flight Hanoi → Da Nang.\n* Check-in & relax a bit.\n* Afternoon: *Hoi An Ancient Town* (best explored in daylight + evening\nlanterns).\n* Evening:\n\n  * *Japanese Covered Bridge*\n  * Tailor shops & souvenirs\n  * *Boat ride on Thu Bon River with lantern release*\n* Night: Return Da Nang.\n\n---------\n\n### *Day 4 – 5 Nov (Da Nang Full Day)*\n\n* Morning: *Ba Na Hills + Sun World* (Golden Bridge, cable car, Fantasy\nPark). Needs \\~5–6 hrs.\n* Return by afternoon/evening.\n* Evening/Night:\n\n  * *My Khe Beach sunset*\n  * *Dragon Bridge Fire Show* (weekends at 9 PM)\n  * Riverside walk.\n\n---------\n\n### *Day 5 – 6 Nov (Da Nang → Singapore)*\n\n* Morning: Fly Da Nang → Singapore.\n* Afternoon: Check-in + rest.\n* Evening:\n\n  * *Gardens by the Bay (Flower Dome + Cloud Forest)*\n  * *OCBC Skywalk*\n  * *Marina Bay Sands SkyPark* for night view.\n\n---------\n\n### *Day 6 – 7 Nov (Sentosa Island)*\n\n* Full day: *Universal Studios* 🎢\n* Late afternoon: *Siloso Beach / Cable Car ride*\n* Evening: *Wings of Time Show* (book tickets).\n\n---------\n\n### *Day 7 – 8 Nov (Singapore City)*\n\n* Morning: *Singapore Zoo OR Jurong Bird Park* (pick ONE, both are\nhalf-day).\n* Afternoon: *Chinatown + Little India* (temples, street shopping, food).\n* Evening:\n\n  * *Clarke Quay* (dinner + nightlife)\n  * *Singapore River Cruise*.\n\n---------\n\n### *Day 8 – 9 Nov (Singapore → Jaipur)*\n\n* Morning: Last-minute shopping at *Orchard Road / Bugis Street*.\n* Flight: Singapore → Jaipur.\n\n\n*Note: *share best lowest possible package with all inclusive - flight,\nvisa, transferred, activities, Hotels, other taxes, charges any etc\n\n*contact*: 9799950555\n\nSachin Goyal',NULL,'2025-09-17 15:58:11','received','<CANZi8W3fMhjw6fyFJbreqz5dpqB+xrBiyLXT-urzNn0x_QKfow@mail.gmail.com>','11787',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(139,NULL,'allysachin@gmail.com','Re: we need tour package with flight and visa for vietnam and singapore','*Date of Travel: *Mid night flight from delhi at: *00:05 AM from delhi*\n\n*for *: 4A + 2 kids(10 year, 3 years)\n\n*Contact numbe*r: 9799950555\n\nOn Wed, Sep 17, 2025 at 9:26 PM allysac4u <allysachin@gmail.com> wrote:\n\n> we need tour package with flight and visa for vietnam and singapore\n>\n> 4A, 2 Kids (10 year, 3 yrs)\n>\n> ### *Day 1 – 2 Nov (Delhi → Hanoi)*\n>\n> * Morning: Arrival & check-in at Old Quarter.\n> * Afternoon (doable in half-day):\n>\n>   * *Ho Chi Minh Complex* (house-on-stilts, museum, One-Pillar Pagoda)\n>   * *Temple of Literature* (Vietnam’s first university)\n> * Evening:\n>\n>   * *Hoan Kiem Lake + Ngoc Son Temple + Huc Bridge*\n>   * Skip Quan Thanh Temple (too much in half day, far from others).\n>   * *Water Puppet Show* (book in advance).\n>\n> ---------\n>\n> ### *Day 2 – 3 Nov (Halong Bay Day Trip)*\n>\n> * Early morning: Drive Hanoi → Halong (\\~2.5–3 hrs).\n> * Cruise from *Tuan Chau Harbor*:\n>\n>   * *Sung Sot Cave (Surprise Cave)*\n>   * *Bo Hon Island*\n>   * *Kayaking or Bamboo Boat*\n>   * *Ti Top Island (panoramic view & beach swim)*\n> * Evening: Return to Hanoi.\n>\n> ---------\n>\n> ### *Day 3 – 4 Nov (Hanoi → Da Nang → Hoi An)*\n>\n> * Early morning: Flight Hanoi → Da Nang.\n> * Check-in & relax a bit.\n> * Afternoon: *Hoi An Ancient Town* (best explored in daylight + evening\n> lanterns).\n> * Evening:\n>\n>   * *Japanese Covered Bridge*\n>   * Tailor shops & souvenirs\n>   * *Boat rid